  "job_B3.2.24_20251003_114627": {
    "text": "Scea\u00fee, for \u00fean ne meaht \u00f0u \u00fea \u00ferowunge gelettan \u00fee f\u00e6der wolde & geteohod h\u00e6fde, \u00fe\u00e6t ic for\nSaga\u00fe o\u00f0er godspellere \u00fe\u00e6t he, ure dryhten, \u00e6thrine \u00fe\u00e6s mannes earan, & he w\u00e6s sona \u00e6fter \u00feam hal\n\u00d0a hie \u00fea Crist oferfangenne h\u00e6fdon, \u00fea gebundon hie hine & l\u00e6ddon \u00e6rest to Annan.\nW\u00e6s se Anna sweor \u00fe\u00e6s Caifan \u00fee \u00f0y gere w\u00e6s bisceop.\nW\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t se ilca Caifas \u00fee \u00e6r \u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6re ge\u00feeahtunge mid Iudeum w\u00e6s, \u00fea hie ymb hine, Crist, spr\u00e6con &\nGif we hine forl\u00e6ta\u00fe, \u00feonne cyrre\u00f0 \u00feis folc to him & on hine gelyfa\u00f0.\nCuma\u00fe Romane & genima\u00fe ure land & ure \u00feeode.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Caifas: Hw\u00e6t la, ge syndon unwise men.\nFor hwan nella\u00fe ge ge\u00feencan \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feis is selre, \u00fe\u00e6tte an man for eall folc dea\u00fe \u00ferowige \u00feonne eall \u00feeod\nWitgode he \u00fe\u00e6t ungewealdene mu\u00f0e be Cristes \u00ferowunge.\nS\u00e6gde so\u00f0, swa he nyste, for \u00fean \u00fee Cristes \u00ferowung & his lichamlic dea\u00f0 \u00feam untrywan folce his \u00feara\n\u00d0a l\u00e6ddon hie hine, Crist, gebundenne in sumne cafertun.\n\u00dea eode Petrus & Iohannes, \u00fee \u00feas drihtenlican \u00ferowonge saga\u00fe, feorran \u00e6fter him.\n\u00dea w\u00e6s he, Iohannes, \u00feam bisceope cu\u00f0 & his mannum; eode \u00fea eac in \u00feone cafertun sona \u00e6fter him.\n\u00dea stod he, Petrus, \u00fe\u00e6rute \u00e6t \u00feam gate, & hine se geatwerd ne wolde in forl\u00e6tan.\n\u00dea eode he eft, Iohannes, to \u00feam geatwearde & gespr\u00e6c \u00fe\u00e6tte he Petrus in forlete.\nW\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t an mennen \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t geat heold.\n\u00dea he \u00fea, Petrus, in eode \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6t geat, \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t mennen to him: Numquid, Ac ne eart \u00f0u \u00feysses\n\u00dea onsoc he sona & cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he his ne w\u00e6re.\n\u00d0a w\u00e6s \u00f0\u00e6r sum fyr on\u00e6led.\n\u00dea stodon hie, \u00fe\u00e6s bisceopes \u00feegnas, \u00fe\u00e6r \u00e6t \u00feam fyre & wyrmdon hie; w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t weder wel col.\n\u00dea stod he, Petrus, \u00e6t \u00f0am fyre & hine wyrmde.\n\u00dea fregn se bisceop & ahsode urne dryhten Crist be his discipulos & be his lare.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, Crist, to him: Ego palam, Hw\u00e6t, ic openlice & undearnunga middangeard l\u00e6rde & symle\n\u00deonne ic hie ealle l\u00e6rde, ne ic owiht dearnunga spr\u00e6c, ne min lar owiht diogol w\u00e6s.\nHw\u00e6t frinest \u00f0u me \u00fe\u00e6s?\nFrin \u00fe\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6s \u00fea men \u00fee min word & mine lare gehyrdon.\nEfne \u00fe\u00e6s \u00fea ilcan \u00fee her ymbutan me standa\u00fe, hie witon hw\u00e6t ic hie l\u00e6rde.\n\u00dea he \u00fea, Crist, \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fea sloh \u00feara bisceopes \u00f0egna sum hine ofer o\u00f0er wange, \u00fee him \u00fe\u00e6r \u00e6tstod,\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Crist to him: Si male locutus sum, Gif ic unteala dyde, swa hit ne sie, find \u00fee gewitnesse & hit\nGif ic teala cw\u00e6\u00f0 & so\u00f0 s\u00e6gde, hw\u00e6t witest \u00f0u me o\u00f0\u00f0e to hwan swingest \u00f0u me?\n\u00dea he \u00fea, Petrus, \u00e6t \u00feam fyre stod, swa ic \u00e6r s\u00e6gde, & hine wyrmde, \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 hiora sum to him: Ac\n\u00dea onsoc he sona swi\u00f0e scearpe & cw\u00e6\u00f0: Ne eom ic discipul, ne ic w\u00e6t hw\u00e6t \u00f0u m\u00e6nest.\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00feara bisceopes \u00f0egna sum, w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6s mannes cu\u00f0a & ge\u00feofta \u00fee Petrus \u00e6r gewundode & him\nAc ne geseah ic \u00fee in \u00feam leactune mid \u00feinum hlaforde?\n\u00dea onsoc he, Petrus, sona eft \u00feriddan si\u00f0e & mid a\u00f0um swor \u00fe\u00e6t he his ne w\u00e6re.\n& \u00fea sona creow hana \u00e6fter \u00feam.\n\u00dea gemunde he, Petrus, \u00fe\u00e6t word \u00fe\u00e6t Crist him \u00e6r to cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t he him sceolde \u00feriwa wi\u00f0sacan \u00e6r\n\u00dea eode Petrus ut \u00feanon & weop swi\u00f0e sare.\n\u00d0a sende he Crist, Anna, gebundenne to Caifan, his m\u00e6ge, \u00fee \u00f0y geare w\u00e6s bysceop.\nS\u00e6g\u00f0 o\u00f0er euuangeliste \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r w\u00e6ron gesomnode \u00feara sacerda ealdermen ealle, & ymb \u00fe\u00e6t spr\u00e6con\n& hine \u00fea l\u00e6ddon in \u00fe\u00e6t gemot beforan hie ealle.\n& eodon manige lease gewitan for\u00f0 & him m\u00e6nig alogen \u00feing ons\u00e6gdon.\n\u00dea aras he, se ealdorman \u00feara sacerda, & cw\u00e6\u00f0 to Criste: For hwan ne ondswerast \u00f0u \u00feyssum mannum\n\u00d0a ne andswarode he him, Crist, \u00e6nige worde.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se ealdorman \u00feara ealdorsacerda eft to him: Ic \u00fee halsige \u00feurh lifigendne God \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u us\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Crist to him: Efne swa \u00f0u cw\u00e6de, swa hit is.\nSo\u00f0 is \u00feonne \u00fe\u00e6t ic eow secge \u00f0\u00e6t nu hw\u00e6nne gelimpe\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t ge geseo\u00f0 mannes sunu sittendne on \u00fea\n\u00d0a hie \u00feas word gehyrdon, \u00fea slat he, se ealdorman \u00feara sacerda, se bisceop, his sylfes hr\u00e6gl, & cw\u00e6\u00f0\nHwylc \u00feearf is us o\u00f0erra gewitnessa?\nHw\u00e6t, we nu \u00e6t his sylfes mu\u00f0e gehyrdon his yfelsunga.\nHw\u00e6t \u00feince\u00f0 eow nu hu we hine scylen deman?\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don hie ealle: Reus est mortis, He is dea\u00fee scyldig.\n& \u00fea spiwon hie hiora spatl on his andwlitan & mid hira handum hine on his wange slogon, & him\n& he \u00fe\u00e6t eall, se heofonlica cyning, for manncynnes h\u00e6lo ge\u00feyldelice ab\u00e6r & ar\u00e6fnode.\n\u00dea s\u00e6gde sanctus Iohannes euangelista \u00fe\u00e6tte hi hine l\u00e6ddon swi\u00f0e \u00e6r on morgen to Pilatus domerne,\n\u00d0a noldon hie, \u00fea Iudeas, \u00fe\u00e6der in to Pilate gangan for hira Eastertidum.\nW\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t hira \u00feeaw \u00fe\u00e6t hie n\u00e6fre woldon in \u00fea tid in \u00e6nig \u00fe\u00e6ra inna in gangan \u00fee h\u00e6\u00f0enes cynnes\n\u00dea wiste Pilatus \u00fe\u00e6t.\n\u00dea eode he in to Iudeum & him to cw\u00e6\u00f0: Hwylce synne seca\u00fe ge to \u00feyssum men?\nFor hwan oncunnon ge hine?\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don hie, \u00fea Iudeas: Si non esset hic malefactor, Gif he n\u00e6re synnig & forworht, \u00feonne ne\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, Pilatus: Accipite, Nima\u00fe ge hine \u00feonne & witnia\u00fe swa eower \u00e6 bebeode\u00f0.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don hie, \u00f0a Iudeas: Nobis non licet, Nis us alyfed \u00fe\u00e6t we moten \u00e6nigne man cwellan on \u00feas\nSceolde \u00fe\u00e6t word bion gefylled, \u00fe\u00e6t he, dryhten h\u00e6lend, \u00e6r sylfa cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t Iudeas, \u00fea \u00fee \u00e6fter his\nFor \u00fean Pilatus & his \u00feegnas \u00fee hine ahengon w\u00e6ron el\u00feeodige men, Romanisces cynnes, for \u00fean\n\u00dea eode he, Pilatus, eft in his domern & het hine, urne dryhten Crist, to him l\u00e6dan, & him to cw\u00e6\u00f0: Tu\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Crist to him: Cwist \u00f0u \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feines \u00feances \u00fee \u00fee o\u00f0re men be me s\u00e6gdon?\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, Pilatus: Ne \u00fe\u00e6t huru is \u00fe\u00e6t ic sie Iudeisc mann, ne ic \u00fee synderlice \u00e6f\u00feancan to wat.\nAc \u00feine agene leode & hira bisceopas \u00fee synnigne secga\u00fe, & for \u00feam hider \u00fee me to cwalme brohton.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, ure h\u00e6lend Crist: Nis min rice hionon of \u00feyssum middangearde.\nW\u00e6re hit, \u00feonne campudun mine \u00feegnas for me, \u00fe\u00e6t ic n\u00e6re Iudeum seald.\nAc nu nis min rice heonon.\nMen \u00fea leofostan, hw\u00e6t m\u00e6nde ure dryhten mid \u00feam wordum, \u00fea he cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t his rice heonon ne\nHw\u00e6t, we witon \u00fe\u00e6tte ealle ricu, \u00e6ghw\u00e6\u00f0er ge heofonlico ge eor\u00f0lico, ge ealle gesceafto on his\nFor \u00f0an nis n\u00e6nig to \u00feam rice her on middangearde \u00fe\u00e6t he dea\u00fe \u00ferowigan ne scile, ac \u00fe\u00e6t eor\u00f0lice\nSwa her on worulde is seo sorh & sio unblis dryhtnes h\u00e6lendes & \u00feara haligra, for \u00fean \u00fee hie on sorge\n\u00dea he \u00fea, Crist, cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t his rice heonon ne w\u00e6re of \u00f0yssum middangearde, \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Pilatus to him:\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Crist to him: So\u00f0 \u00feu segest, cining ic eom.\n& to \u00feam ic w\u00e6s in woruld acenned & to \u00feam cwom in middangeard, \u00fe\u00e6t ic wolde so\u00f0e gewitnesse\nFor \u00feam \u00e6lc \u00feara manna \u00fee so\u00f0 & riht gelyfe\u00f0, & \u00e6lc \u00feara \u00fee min word & mine stefne gehyre\u00f0, se\n\u00dea he \u00fea, ure dryhten, \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fea eode he, Pilatus, eft ut to \u00feam Iudeum & him to cw\u00e6\u00f0: Ne m\u00e6g ic\nIc \u00feonne wat \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feis is eower \u00feeaw & eower gewuna, \u00fe\u00e6t ic eow sceal in \u00feas eowre Eastertide anum\nWilla\u00fe ge \u00fe\u00e6t ic eow agife \u00feysne eowerne cyning & \u00fe\u00e6t ge him feorh forgifen?\nWiste he, Pilatus, genog geare \u00fe\u00e6tte hie, \u00fea Iudeas, for \u00e6fste anum Crist hatedon.\n\u00dea cleopedon hie sona, \u00fea Iudeas, ealle ane worde & \u00feus cw\u00e6don: Ne willa\u00fe we \u00feysne, ac we willa\u00fe\nW\u00e6s se Barrabas haten sum scea\u00fea & forwyrht man, w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6r \u00fey si\u00f0e on bendum.\n\u00dea b\u00e6don hie, \u00fea Iudeas, \u00fe\u00e6t him man \u00feone agefe \u00fe\u00e6t hi moston him feorg forgifan.\n\u00dea heht he, Pilatus, Crist swingan, & hie genamon, \u00fea milite, & geworhton \u00feyrnene coronan & setton\n\u00dea genamon hie, for \u00fean, bysmernesse, & geworhton \u00fe\u00e6t tacen of \u00feornum & setton on his heafod, &\n\u00dea genamon hie, for \u00fean, \u00fea bysmernesse, & gegiredon hine, urne dryhten h\u00e6lende Crist, mid reade\n& hi hine mid hira handum on his wange slogon & him m\u00e6nigfealde bysmernessa dydon.\n& he \u00fea \u00feis eall, se heofonlica f\u00e6der, ge\u00f0eldelice & eadmodlice for us \u00ferowode & ab\u00e6r.\n\u00dea eode he, Pilatus, eft ut to Iudeum & him to cw\u00e6\u00f0: Nu gyt ic hine hate l\u00e6dan hider ut beforan eow\n\u00dea eode he, ure dryhten Crist, ut beforan \u00fea Iudeas.\nH\u00e6fde he \u00fea \u00feyrnenne coronan on his heafde, & mid \u00feam readan hr\u00e6gle gegyred w\u00e6s.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, Pilatus, to Iudeum: Ecce homo, \u00deis is se man he; ac hata\u00fe hine nu ateon swa swa ge\n\u00dea hie \u00fea hine gesawon, \u00fea cleopodon hie sona ealle ane worde & \u00feus cw\u00e6don: Crucifige, crucifige,\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, Pilatus, to him: Nima\u00fe ge hine \u00feonne & aho\u00fe hine.\nNe m\u00e6g ic \u00e6nigne incan on him metan, \u00fe\u00e6t ic wite for hwan ic hine yflian scyle.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don \u00fea Iudeas: We habba\u00fe \u00e6, & \u00e6fter ure \u00e6 he sceal dea\u00f0 \u00ferowian, for \u00fean \u00fee he s\u00e6gde \u00fe\u00e6t he\n\u00dea he \u00fea, Pilatus, \u00feas word gehyrde, \u00fea ondred he him & w\u00e6s forht geworden.\n& \u00fea eode he eft in \u00fe\u00e6t domern & \u00fea heht Crist to him & him to cw\u00e6\u00f0: Unde es tu?, Gesaga me\n\u00dea ne geandswarode he him, Crist ure dryhten, \u00e6nige worde.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, Pilatus: For hwan ne andswarast \u00feu me?\nAc ne wast \u00feu \u00fe\u00e6t ic h\u00e6bbe mihte \u00fe\u00e6t ic \u00fee m\u00e6g ahon, swa ic h\u00e6bbe mihte \u00fe\u00e6t ic \u00fee m\u00e6g forl\u00e6tan?\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Crist dryhten ure to him: Ne hafast \u00f0u \u00e6nige mihte wi\u00f0 me nym\u00fee \u00fee sie ufan geseald; - efne\n\u00dea \u00feohte he, Pilatus, \u00fe\u00e6t he scolde urne dryhten Crist forl\u00e6tan & him feorh forgifan.\n\u00d0a \u00fea Iudeas \u00fe\u00e6t ongeton, \u00fea cleopodon hie & cw\u00e6don: Gif \u00f0u \u00feysne man forl\u00e6test & hine ne h\u00e6tst\nFor \u00feam \u00e6lc \u00feara manna \u00fee hine sylfne to cyninge de\u00f0, \u00feonne wi\u00f0cwi\u00f0 he Caseres wordum.\n\u00d0a he \u00fea, Pilatus, \u00feas word gehyrde, \u00fe\u00e6t he n\u00e6re Caseres freond butan he hine cwellan hete, \u00fea ges\u00e6t\n& he \u00fea \u00fewoh his handa & cw\u00e6\u00f0 to Iudeum: Wita\u00fe ge nu \u00fe\u00e6t ic wille beon \u00feyses mannes blodes\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don hie, \u00fea Iudeas: Sanguis eius, Sie his blod ofer us & ofer ure bearn.\nB\u00e6don swi\u00f0e unl\u00e6dlicre bene, swa him sy\u00fe\u00fean eall unl\u00e6dlic on becwom.\nW\u00e6s \u00feis eall geworden on hira Eastertide.\nWeor\u00f0edon hie \u00fea tiid swi\u00f0e.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, Pilatus, to Iudeum: Ecce rex uester, \u00feis is eower cyning.\nAc hu willa\u00fe ge hine ateon?\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don hie ealle: Tolle, tolle, crucifige eum, Nim \u00feu hine, nim & hat hine niman, & hat hine ahon.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, Pilatus: Hw\u00e6t, ic \u00feonne hate eowerne cyning ahon?\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don hie, Iudeas: Ne habba\u00fe we \u00e6nigne cyning butan Casere.\n\u00dea w\u00e6s \u00e6fter \u00feam wordum \u00fe\u00e6t he, Pilatus, urne dryhten Crist Iudeum agef, & sealde his agene men\n\u00dea namon hie hine & l\u00e6ddon to \u00fe\u00e6re stowe \u00fe\u00e6r hie hine eft on ahengon.\n& he sylfa b\u00e6r \u00fea rode sumne d\u00e6l \u00fe\u00e6s weges \u00fee hine man eft on aheng.\n\u00dea \u00e6fter \u00feam ahengon hie hine on \u00feam clife \u00fee hie heton Golgo\u00f0\u00f0a, & twegen scea\u00f0an him on \u00fea twa\n\u00dea wrat he, Pilatus, sum gewrit on brede, & \u00fe\u00e6t het gef\u00e6stnian onufan \u00fea Cristes rode.\nW\u00e6s \u00f0us awriten: Iesus Nazarenus, \u00deis is h\u00e6lend se Nadzarenisca, Iudea cyning.\nW\u00e6s hit awriten on \u00fereo ge\u00feeode, \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6s on Ebrisc & on Crecisc & on L\u00e6denisc.\n& m\u00e6nige Iudeas \u00fe\u00e6t gewrit r\u00e6ddon, for \u00fean sio stow w\u00e6s wel neah Hierusalem \u00fe\u00e6re byrig \u00fee he on\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don \u00fea bisceopas to Pilate: Ne writ \u00fe\u00e6t gewrit \u00fe\u00e6t he sie cyning, ac writ \u00fe\u00e6t he sylfa cw\u00e6de\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, Pilatus: \u00de\u00e6t ic \u00fe\u00e6r wrat, \u00fe\u00e6t sceal swa awriten bion.\n\u00dea genamon hie, \u00fea milite, \u00fea hie Crist urne dryhten ahangenne h\u00e6fdon, & \u00fea tod\u00e6ldon hie his hr\u00e6gl\n& \u00fea gita w\u00e6s his tunuce onsundran untod\u00e6led.\nW\u00e6s sio tunuce syllice geworht: n\u00e6s n\u00e6nig seam on, ac w\u00e6s eall on anum awefen.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don hie: Uton, la, ne toslitan \u00fea tunecan, ac utan hleotan hwylc ure hie agan scyle.\n& \u00fea dydon hie swa.\nSceolde se witedom beon gefylled se \u00fee \u00e6r in \u00feam sealme awriten w\u00e6s & awitgod, & se halga gast\nW\u00e6ron \u00fea milite \u00fe\u00e6s gerefan men \u00fey \u00fe\u00e6t dydon.\n\u00dea stod \u00fe\u00e6r Cristes h\u00e6lendes licumlic modor, sancta Maria, & hire sweostor mid hire, & Maria\n\u00dea he \u00fea, Crist, of \u00fe\u00e6re rode geseah \u00fea his modor \u00fe\u00e6r \u00e6tstandan & his \u00feone leofan \u00feegn, \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he,\n& \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he eft to his \u00feam leofan \u00feegne: Ecce mater, \u00deis is \u00fein modor, & \u00feu hie \u00fee for modor hafa.\n& he \u00fea, Iohannes, swa dyde, & he hie \u00fea in moderlufan h\u00e6fde.\nW\u00e6s hit midd\u00e6g \u00fea hie hine on rode hengon.\n& \u00fea he on rode ahangen w\u00e6s, \u00fea ge\u00feystrode hit & efne f\u00e6stlice genihtode ofer eallne middangeard\n& sio sunne & ealle \u00fea heofontungulu hira leoht betyndon & behyddon, \u00fe\u00e6t hie \u00fe\u00e6t mor\u00f0or geseon ne\n\u00dea wiste he, ure dryhten Crist, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea \u00feing gefylled w\u00e6ron ealle \u00fee be his \u00ferowunge awritene &\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he \u00fea gita: Sitio, & s\u00e6de \u00fe\u00e6t hine \u00feyrste.\n\u00dea w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6r sum f\u00e6t mid ecede gefylled.\n\u00dea genamon hie sume spingan & gefyldon mid ecede & ysopan \u00fea wyrt utan befeoldon, & dydon on\nSceolde se witedom bion gefylled \u00fee \u00e6r in \u00feam sealme awriten & awitgod w\u00e6s be \u00feyssum ylcan\n\u00dea he \u00f0a, Crist, \u00fe\u00e6s ecedes onbyrgde, \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, Crist: Nu syndon gefylled halige gewrito.\n\u00dea onhylde he his heafod on o\u00f0ere eaxle & \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6ne gast of \u00feam lichoman onsende.\n\u00dea noldon hie, \u00fea Iudeas, for heora Eastertidum \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea lic ealne d\u00e6g on \u00fe\u00e6re rode w\u00e6ren, for \u00feam hie\nEodon \u00fea for\u00fe to Pilate & b\u00e6don hine \u00fe\u00e6t he hete \u00feara manna sceancan brecan on \u00fe\u00e6re rode, \u00fe\u00e6t hie\n\u00dea het he, Pilatus, swa don: het gan his men to.\n\u00dea forbr\u00e6con hie \u00feara twega scea\u00feena sceancan \u00fee mid Criste hangedon; hie begen \u00fea gita lifgende\n\u00dea hie \u00fea to Criste comon, \u00fea gesawon hie \u00fe\u00e6t he w\u00e6s for\u00fefered on \u00fe\u00e6re rode.\nFor \u00feam ne br\u00e6con hie his ban, ac genam \u00feara cempena an & mid his spere his sidan wundode, & \u00fea\n\u00de\u00e6t tacnode h\u00e6lo middangeardes, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0urh his blod fulwihtw\u00e6ter gewyr\u00fean sceolde.\n& he sylf cw\u00e6\u00f0, sanctus Iohannes: \u00deas gewitnesse ic secge, efne swa ic hit minum eagum geseah.\n& ic wat \u00fe\u00e6t sio min gewitnes is so\u00f0, & ic hit for \u00feam eow secge \u00fe\u00e6t ic wille \u00fe\u00e6t ge hit so\u00f0 gelyfen.\nW\u00e6s \u00feis eal to \u00f0am geworden - \u00fe\u00e6t hie \u00fea his ban ne br\u00e6con & hie hine mid \u00fey spere in \u00fea sidan\nSwylce eft o\u00f0er gewrit cw\u00e6\u00f0: Uidebunt in quem transfixerunt, Hie besawon \u00fea in \u00feone \u00fee hie\n\u00dea w\u00e6s Ioseph haten sum man Arema\u00f0\u00f0ia \u00fe\u00e6re byrig.\nW\u00e6s welig man for worulde, & he w\u00e6s eac for Gode so\u00f0f\u00e6st & god.\nW\u00e6s he digolice Cristes h\u00e6lendes \u00feegn, & he elcor ne dorste for Iudea ege.\n\u00dea iode he to Pilate & b\u00e6d hine \u00fe\u00e6t he moste geniman \u00fe\u00e6s h\u00e6lendes lichoman & bebyrgan.\n\u00dea lyfde he, Pilatus, him \u00fe\u00e6t.\n\u00dea com \u00fe\u00e6r \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6s h\u00e6lendes \u00feegn Nicodemus w\u00e6s haten.\nBrohte \u00fe\u00e6r sume smyrenesse swi\u00f0e swete of myrran & of o\u00f0rum deorwyr\u00feum wyrtum, & geworhte\n\u00dea genamon hie Cristes h\u00e6lendes lichoman & hine adune adydon, & hine ealne gesmyredon mid \u00feam\n\u00dea h\u00e6fde Ioseph se goda man him sylfum niwe byrgene geworhte, in anum swi\u00f0e myclum stane\n\u00dea genamon hie for \u00feam ofeste, & gesetton \u00fe\u00e6s h\u00e6lendes lichoman in \u00fea byrgenne.\nMen \u00fea leofestan, hw\u00e6t, ure drihten \u00e6lmihtig God, \u00fea his haliga lichama in \u00fea halgan byrgenne\nAc utan we nu for \u00fean a singalice ussum dryhtne h\u00e6lendan Criste \u00feanc secgan eallre \u00fe\u00e6re\nUtan we hine nu lufigan ofer eall o\u00f0re \u00feing, swa we nu gehyra\u00fe \u00fe\u00e6t he us lufode & us hyldo to",
